// Glowcave: magma breach.
//
// A dark cavern lit only by blue glowshroom clusters, violet crystal spikes
// and lava. At first it is calm: mist drifts off the shore of a black lake
// and water drips from the stalactites. At tick 290 the obsidian plug that
// holds back a magma chamber is blown out with a flash, and its red-hot
// fragments fly out over the cave as glowing particles. The lava pours down
// a stepped ramp. It holds a lot of heat and gives off latent heat before it
// freezes, so it stays molten all the way down, and the rock beside it glows
// where it heats by conduction. Where it runs into the lake the water flashes
// to steam; the obsidian skin crumbles to gravel and sinks, so fresh lava
// keeps reaching the water and the steam plume keeps rising. The feeder in the chamber
// roof is cut off at tick 480, so the flow thins and dims from yellow toward
// red as it cools. At tick 1100 blasts cut the neck of a ceiling slab
// studded with crystals: it falls as a rigid body, its crystals still lighting
// the cave around it, and plunges into the lake, throwing the water up over
// it. At tick 720 a flooded fissure in the roof over the ramp cracks open,
// and a waterfall pours onto the lava, boiling off in a column of steam while
// the lava under it crusts black. In the aftermath a stalactite over the cooling
// front starts to drip.
// A light draft carries the steam out over the lake.
[scene]
name = glowcave
description = Magma breaks into a dark cavern lit by glowing fungus and crystals: the plug blows out in a shower of sparks, lava runs down a stepped ramp and quenches in the lake in a rising steam plume, its crust crumbling to gravel, then a crystal-studded slab breaks from the ceiling and plunges into the water.
size = 960 576
seed = 0x91c4
ticks = 1800
wind = 2

